{#- The RTL outputs describe the design's own modules. At this point every primitive library a
    flow read with `-lib` is in the design as boxes, and a box can keep its `always` blocks, which
    `write_json` refuses to write (`Module ALU contains processes`). The default selection holds
    no box, so `-selected` writes the design's modules only, as `write_verilog` and `show` do.
    Every block ends its last command with a newline, so an including template that strips the
    whitespace after the include cannot join the next command to it.
    yosys scripts have no `exit` command: `stop_after == "rtl"` is handled by the including
    template, which simply does not emit the post-RTL commands. -#}
{% if settings.rtl_json -%}
log -stdout Writing JSON {{settings.rtl_json}}
write_json -selected {{settings.rtl_json|path}}
{% endif -%}
{% if settings.rtl_verilog -%}
log -stdout Writing Verilog {{settings.rtl_verilog}}
write_verilog {{settings.rtl_verilog|path}}
{% endif -%}
{% if settings.rtl_graph -%}
log -stdout Writing RTL graph to {{settings.rtl_graph.with_suffix('.dot')}}
show -prefix {{settings.rtl_graph.with_suffix("")|verbatim_path}} -format dot {{settings.rtl_graph_flags|join(" ")}}
{% endif -%}
